          <div class="quiet-work__title">
            <small>{project.field}</small>
            <h3>{project.title}</h3>
          </div>
          <p>{project.description}</p>
          <div class="quiet-work__proof">
            <strong>{project.proof}</strong>
            <small>{project.proofLabel}</small>
          </div>
          <span class="quiet-work__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="quiet-trust" aria-labelledby="quiet-trust-title">
    <p class="quiet-kicker">The practice</p>
    <div class="quiet-trust__body">
      <h2 id="quiet-trust-title">Research economist.<br />Teacher. Builder.</h2>
      <div class="quiet-trust__copy">
        <p>
          I work best where a problem does not fit neatly inside one discipline. The same structural instinct runs
          through econometrics, strategy, networks, remote sensing, geospatial socioeconomics, mathematics, and
          learning. It also extends into my independent work with acoustics, signals, and sound.
        </p>
        <p class="quiet-trust__credentials">
          PhD, Economics · MS, GIS · doctoral minor, Quantitative Psychology · St. Louis / worldwide
        </p>
        <nav aria-label="Learn more about Ian">
